  <i>She was in grave trouble. Because this male was not just some new arrival, he was Maxheim Skolov: second-in-command of one of the most powerful crime families in the galaxy. The exacting mastermind behind the empire. And he was here to kill her for what she’d done to his fellow Brotherhood members. The darkness inside her returned with a vengeance.</i>
</b><br><br><i>Savage Prince</i> was fast-paced, action-packed, intense, and smokin' hot :-) The key qualities that describe Alison Aimes' writing style are all present here: electric, energetic, &amp; compelling. While this book has dark elements (<input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="6481cb1a-7bbf-4ab1-a5ea-3f84be856355" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="6481cb1a-7bbf-4ab1-a5ea-3f84be856355">: graphic murder, violence, sex trafficking, &amp; abuse (but not from the hero)</label>, the overall story has heart. The H is an alphahole, but one who caves to his Omega. Omegaverse readers who like dominating/possessive Alphas will love Maxheim. I found him very likable. I <i>loved</i> Tess. I like that she came from an underprivileged background. I felt the author delved into her psychology, and really thought about how someone like Tess would have learned to survive &amp; cope in her circumstances. She has a cynical exterior, but vulnerable core. <br><br>I was delighted to see a Dread Pirate Roberts twist in the plot regarding the villain! <br><br><img src="https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1624577641ra/31543749.gif" width="640" height="330" alt="description" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br><br><img src="https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1624577710ra/31543751.gif" width="585" height="285" alt="description" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>Those who have watched <i>The Princess Bride</i> &amp; have read this book will hopefully get my meaning. I'm not elaborating to prevent spoiling :) <br><br>Btw the word <i>
  <b>Mine</b>
</i> in this book is basically the equivalent of this:<br><br><img src="https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1624577839ra/31543754.gif" width="560" height="360" alt="description" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>Maxheim totally goes caveman around Tess, but in reality he's putty in her hands and will go to great lengths to have her. <br><br>Overall I recommend this book to Omegaverse readers, especially those who like scifi or mafia - and especially those who like this kind of Alpha/omega trope. The author is nailing it in this series. <br><br><b>Trigger Warnings</b>: <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="7793f1fb-8f2e-4494-8111-f9e1308e8329" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="7793f1fb-8f2e-4494-8111-f9e1308e8329">Graphic murder, graphic violence, abuse (not from the H)</label><br><b>Safety</b>: <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="9a762bb4-cb5e-4545-b152-eb7bbefc37af" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="9a762bb4-cb5e-4545-b152-eb7bbefc37af">No cheating, no ow drama. The H is possessive &amp; centered on the Omega. Not even a mention of past relationships/hook ups.</label><br><b>HEA</b>: Yes. This book is a standalone &amp; ends with a HEA. <br><br>*Note: While this book can be read first in the series (this is a standalone series) you'll get more context and backstory regarding the twins, the Skolov brothers, and the Brotherhood if you've at least read book 1, Ruthless King. With that said, if you start with this book you'll understand the main romance between the couple just fine - they both meet for the first time in this book. Just other elements to the plot that I mentioned above first start to develop in book 1.<br><br>*ARC kindly provided by the author</["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></["br"]></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/81374210?shelf=escorts-strippers-sex-workers" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">escorts-strippers-sex-workers</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/81374210?shelf=mafia" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">mafia</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/81374210?shelf=omegaverse" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">omegaverse</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">30 likes</span></button></div><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">6 comments</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7