9163i/30047654.jpg" alt="Untitled design-High-Quality" width="686" height="88" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><img src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1598991425i/30047740.gif" alt="My Review" width="468" height="60" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>I enjoyed this a lot it’s a Sci-fi fantasy omegaverse and part of a series this one is about the brother from the previous book Maxheim he’s the fixer of the family always in control of his emotions that is until he runs into his fated-mate in the most unexpected of places and she manages to turn his ordered world upside down.<br>Tess is an omega slave with a very powerful gift one she can use as a weapon when Maxheim appears at the latest omega auction on the trail of his sibling's kidnapper he instantly recognises her as his own and sets about claiming her.<br>Discovering then that their lives are more intertwined than they could realise and that there are others who also want Tess Maxheim definitely has his work cut out keeping her hidden and safe.<br>There’s a death squad on their tail and the brotherhood also wants Tess handed over for her part in their men’s deaths.<br><br>Maxheim surprised me the way he wanted Tess to choose him and not just take but also give and though his dominant protective nature sometimes got in the way of his sense he really did try to give Tess choices whenever possible winning her over with his care and obvious regard.<br>Tess was initially suspicious of course her background doesn’t breed trust easily and with further revelations coming forth about those she trusted blindly she does naturally start to question her own judgement.<br><br>This was intense and super hot these two had so much chemistry together it projected off the page.<br>Tess was actually quite reasonable she wasn’t a drama Queen which I liked she wasn’t one of those heroines that like to act stupidly and make rash decisions and I liked how she realised how lucky she was in Maxheim as a mate. her one flaw was not realising her own worth and thinking that her only value was that of a bargaining chip placing herself as less important. Maxheim well he was just so lickable and totally delicious.<br><br>This was a great addition to the series and I enjoyed it a lot, it was action-packed throughout and the heat levels were through the roof I definitely recommend this it’s very imaginative with some great world-building.<br>I voluntary reviewed a copy of Savage Prince (Ruthless Warlords #2).<br><br><img src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1598991966i/30047768.gif" alt="Untitled design" width="686" height="88" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>Reviewed By Beckie Bookworm<br><a target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" href="https://www.facebook.com/beckiebookworm/">https://www.facebook.com/beckiebookworm/</a><br><a target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" href="http://www.beckiebookworm.com">www.beckiebookworm.com</a></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/9460945?shelf=aliens-creature-monster-non-human" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">aliens-creature-monster-non-human</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/9460945?shelf=arc" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">arc</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/9460945?shelf=book-reviews" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">book-reviews</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span> <div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium" aria-label="Show all items in the list"><span class="Button__labelItem">...more</span></button></