12.477 1.34327C12.4269 1.19375 12.3095 1.0764 12.16 1.02625C11.8966 0.937894 11.6114 1.07983 11.523 1.34327L8.91088 9.13158H0.503157C0.33975 9.13158 0.186521 9.21094 0.0922364 9.3444C-0.0680877 9.57134 -0.0140806 9.88529 0.212865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined-1small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined-1small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4927521055">August 18, 2022</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted"><b>3.5 stars </b> <br /><br />It wasn’t as exciting as I thought it would be and as some reviewers pointed out, this could get/did get quite slow and boring at times <b>but </b>for me it was the perfect in the sense that the hero was great. <br /><br />I don’t read omegaverse and I don’t read dark romance where the relationship between the two leads is dark. The thing is, I love dark romance but mostly what that means in this genre is that there is cnc, dub con, humiliating scenes, control/punishment type of situations etc, and I’d rather drink bleach than read about a “love story” like that. Ok, so having said that, I always look for dark stories where the element of darkness is outside the main relationship and this was one of them. <br /><br />The hero was absolutely great and totally devoted to the heroine once he met her. Out of all the brothers he was the most quiet, reserved and emotionless one which makes his actions here even more telling. He appreciated the heroine for everything she was and he listened to her ideas, her plans etc. - I know it sounds like bare minimum but within the fiction world of this book, women are not seen or heard unless they need to be used for something. That’s literally how every man (father, brother, stranger) treats women so the fact that the hero doesn’t even contemplate his status as a man against her as a woman does give him a lot of points. Compared to the first book and the first hero this was great. <br /><br />I do have one complaint thought. I have read and will read a lot of romance books with crude language and it doesn’t bother me. At all. I like the directness of it. But here, the language used goes beyond crude. And it’s like that in all 3 books. To be honest it’s gross. The same things can be said a little different, without censure but also without making me cringe while reading.<br /><br />Anyway, I read the 3rd book by this point as well. And it’s very much like this one as opposed to being like the 1st one. </span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/97546350?shelf=2022-reads" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">2022-reads</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/97546350?shelf=alien-romance" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">alien-romance</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/97546350?shelf=dark-themes" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">dark-themes</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span> <div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium" aria-lab