ng just fine without feeling like you’re floundering for information usually fed to the reader during book one.<br /><br />This book when invited to read it, promised an engaging enemies-to-lovers, forced proximity, dark, mafia, sci-fi, paranormal romance. A lot to fit into one book, for sure. But not impossible. It’s all about balance to combine all of these things to produce a sensual, romantic, angsty, steamy book that quite literally, is out of this world. Alison has achieved said balance with Savage Prince.<br /><br />As promised to us in the very book title, our main male is indeed, Savage, and is by far my favourite character besides his omega. Maxheim truly is an impressively complex character, you both want to rush to his side and give him a firm lashing with your tongue at the same time. He doesn’t conform to the typical alpha-male attitude, but becomes his true self when his omega comes into his life. This gives a very human-like quality to a very inhuman like male. Simply stellar! <br /><br />One element I would like to praise especially, is the vastness and the expanse of how the story started out from caged beginnings, to where we leave the characters at the end of the book. As infinite as the sci-fi genre is, there also runs the risk of falling into the same storyline, plot and story arc. I’m always somewhat hesitant to read a sci-fi romance because of this. However, this was not the case with Savage Prince, and I couldn’t believe the places that I was taken during this read with the settings, scenes and events. More was packed into this book than the contents of Maxheim’s impressive laced trews, yet it didn’t feel overwhelming or that there was too much to digest. There was always something gripping and engaging to keep you turning those pages, rather than pausing for a breather.<br /><br />I found it hard to put the book down to get a night’s sleep, as I wanted to keep journeying across the stars with our two main characters. Cannot praise Alison highly enough for reader-book engagement, fabulous work!<br /><br />Which leads me onto my next point. Mystery. Just when I thought I had a plot twist figured out, I was caught completely by surprise by something that had been leaving me guessing until everything I thought I knew was turned upside down on its head. Where it’s nice to feel you can predict and guess points within the novel that will happen at a later date, it’s even more rewarding to be proven wrong, caught off guard and surprised. That, for me, is what makes a book truly interesting and I couldn’t keep my jaw closed a the moments of true shock and awe.<br /><br />Savage Prince was prolific in both sad, tense, mysterious and steamy scenes that delivered so much more than the average novel. During the sad scenes, I wept tears along with our omega. During tense, angsty scenes, I was right up in my ebook shouting at our alpha as if he could hear me. During the steamy scenes, I grabbed my nearest fan an hunkered down to read some more. This is a book that truly has it all and has it all in spades, doing nothing by half measures. <br /><br />To sum up, I’m really am glad that I took a chance on a read outside of my go-to genre. I’ve dabbled in the occasional sci-fi romance, only few of them 1% as steamy as Savage Prince, but none have left me as impressed and wanting to read more than this one. <br /><br />Alison Aimes, you’ve earned yourself a new reader and one who’s looking forward to the rest of the books in this series. Five stellar stars for you!</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">5 likes</span></button></div><div clas