tion class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">This is the 2nd book that I've read by this author.. The first book I read by her was back in 2018, and I gotta say this chick can write. She can write some down right heinous, highly charged, and sexually/emotionally intense scenes in her books.. The plot and plights are beyond intriguing and keeps you invested.. BUT-this is the 2nd book where her FMC worked my nerves to no end.. Granted this book's FMC was way better that the previous 2018 book's FMC ( I gave that book just 3 stars) but still, this one skirted the edge of <i>I'm too stupid &amp; emotionally stunted for my own good~</i> for way too long in this story, IMO... <br><br>If you want the FMCs actions and thought processes to make sense of why she's gun shy for as long as she was here, then please DO NOT show me all this transparency in action and intention with the MMC! It annoys me to no end when the MMC is transparent about his intentions and feelings to the FMC CONSISTENTLY, in word and action, but she's still acting like she can't trust him. UGH!!! This creams my corn and pisses me off to no end!! <b>STOP WRITING FEMALES LIKE THIS!</b> And if you must, then make it make sense &amp; be within reason! M'kay?? Thank you! Geez! <br><br>Maxheim Skolov- You have my heart. You have my loyalty. And you have my 💦💦💦<br><br>So, as you can see this FMC was why this book did not get a 5 star nod from me.. <br><img src="https://images.gr-assets.com/photos/1785160005p8/4504400.jpg" width="400" height="400" alt="DBA/" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br>The FMC started off strong and her hesitancy in the beginning was warranted and understandable. But because so much happens back to back, and her seeing and hearing Maxheim's truth where she is concerned, to me, it took her way too long to get on board considering their set of circumstances surrounding them, and what was clearly developing between them personally..<br><br>That aside, this was full of mystery, heartbreak, intense action sequences and the bonds of love, loyalty, and family.. I have to say I love the original concept here of a series based in the sci-fi alien realm, but has tones of the Russian Mafia genre as well.. I've never read a fusion of genres in this way until this book.. So I really enjoyed this.. You care about the folks and their plights. The mystery and intrigue pulls you in. But you stay for the individuals and their cares that they are contending with..<br><br>I am committed to reading the other books in this series.. I need to go back and read book 1 first, though.. <br><br><br>Would I recommend?=Yes<br>Spice?=🌶️🌶️🌶️🌶️🌶️🌶️🌶️<br>Plot/Plight?=4.5<br>MCs?=It's complicated(see above)<br>Ending/Epilogue?=4.5 </span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">8 likes</span></button></div><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">7 comments</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.603