ull,"commentCount":0},"User:31389778":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":31389778,"imageUrlSquare":"","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":0,"textReviewsCount":45,"name":"Margo","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/31389778-margo","contributor":null,"id":31389778},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AAUKVLTDMD1PI":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AAUKVLTDMD1PI"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AAUKVLTDMD1PI\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AAUKVLTDMD1PI","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AAUKVLTDMD1PI"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/31389778?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3969021033"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.Hx5Rz7-Ic0rtQr_r8KEx-g":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.Hx5Rz7-Ic0rtQr_r8KEx-g","creator":{"__ref":"User:31389778"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1624811535131,"createdAt":1623458377748,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1623459275339,"text":"Wahoo! What a great way to spend the evening! In this world there are Alphas who lead, Betas who follow and Omegas who submit. Tess is an Omega and wants out of her nightmare of a situation, along with her friends. I was immediately taken with Tess, her strength and her desire to help others. She is being used for her “gift” to hurt others and even though she doesn’t want to, she doesn’t have a choice in the matter. In comes Maxheim, not your typical Alpha, but all Alpha in all the ways we want in this well written romance. He has been working hard to write a wrong from years past and Tess is not what he needs right now. It messes up all his plans. Yet, Maxheim is much happier with Tess. He does all he can to keep her. I really enjoyed the story line and how it progressed. A few pleasant surprises along the way that made the romance story line unique. I really enjoyed it and look forward to the next book in the series. Highly recommend. ","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AAUKVLTDMD1PI\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j\"}}"},"likeCount":8,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:98512744":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":98512744,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1764079992i/98512744._CR26,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":228,"textReviewsCount":984,"name":"JD (on semi-hiatus)","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/98512744-jd-on-semi-hiatus","contributor":null,"id":98512744},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A37V9I552BX9K8":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A37V9I552BX9K8"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A37V9I552BX9K8\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A37V9I552BX9K8","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A37V9I552BX9K8"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/98512744?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"interesting","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/98512744?shelf=interesting"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"likeable-characters","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/98512744?shelf=likeable-characters"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"mutual-respect","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/98512744?shelf=mutual-respect"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"repetitious","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/98512744?shelf=repetitious"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"strong-heroine","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/98512744?shelf=strong-heroine"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4056566038"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.jL24eOvaTesKACiHh8qKGQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.jL24eOvaTesKACiHh8qKGQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:98512744"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1670000206256,"createdAt":1624592706318,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1625558370822,"text":"This is the second in Ms. Aimes' Omegaverse series set in a galaxy far, far away. Corrupt governments, warring mafia families, and Alpha/Omega dynamics make \u003cs\u003eAnarchy\u003c/s\u003e Anarcheim a dangerous place to live, and few survive unscathed. Although this is a standalone in terms of the couple, the siblings we follow, most of the world-building, and one over-arching line of action were introduced first in \u003ca href=\"https://goodreads.com/book/show/55919400.Ruthless_King__Ruthless_Warlords__1_\" title=\"Ruthless King (Ruthless Warlords #1) by Alison Aimes\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eRuthless King\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eHere, we get second brother, control-freak Maxheim, and Tess, the slave he falls in love with. Although their attraction is very Omegaverse-instant, will Tess' close relationship with the man who nearly destroyed Maxheim's family tear them apart?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI enjoyed this book and recommend it highly -- particularly if you like Omegaverse, but don't like how brutally Alphas treat their Omegas in many of them. Maxheim clearly adores Tess, will do anything for her, and never harms her. I also appreciate that Omegas have more agency in this series than they usually do; thus, Tess is equally appealing: her deprived childhood, low caste, and problematic \"gift\" make it difficult for her to trust Maxheim's feelings; once she does, it was a pleasure watching her come into her own -- finding happiness she never thought she'd have and a strength she didn't know she possessed. The MC, in fact, is this book's strength. Omegaverse is often saturated with long descriptions of animalistic sex (don't worry, some are present here), but, in order to invest in a couple, I need to see some other connection between them; this occurs here when each helps the other process past traumas in healthier ways. Finally (in terms of the couple), their conflict was organic, high-stakes, and seemingly insurmountable since it rests on competing loyalties -- which held this reader's interest throughout.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe rest of the narrative was equally compelling: we find out more about the main mystery and the book ends with a couple of twists I didn't see coming. There are also a couple of poignant emotional moments that, while some were difficult to read, added depth to the usual Omegaverse/Mafia generic tropes.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis would easily have been a five-star rating without the constant repetition that led to unnecessary length -- the same problem I had with the previous book. I wish that authors understood that readers really can retain information: I didn't, for example, need to be reminded of Tess's motivations quite so many times, read another scene of Maxheim's siblings dissecting his personality, or told so often that the family's position within the Brotherhood was difficult.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e4 stars. Third brother Alexi will get the next book. Note: The masks at the beginning have new meaning in the age of Covid.","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A37V9I552BX9K8\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j\"}}"},"likeCount":8,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:79319713":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":79319713,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1752195813i/79319713._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":395,"textReviewsCount":1939,"name":"Kate V","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/79319713-kate-v","contributor":null,"id":79319713},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2LQ3K24PK0GM3":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2LQ3K24PK0GM3"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2LQ3K24PK0GM3\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.i0mlg7-UHTGZwEh4\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2LQ3K24PK0GM3","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2LQ3K24PK0GM3"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.i0mlg7-UHTGZwEh4","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.i0mlg7-UHTGZwEh4"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/79319713?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3804345384"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.jcabIObMw81FNFY7zphQBA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.jcabIObMw81FNFY7zphQBA","creator":{"__ref":"User:79319713"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1686885417185,"createdAt":1624462863135,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1624463348172,"text":"4.75 stars!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis is the second book in the Ruthless Warlords series and I LOVED IT. This story features Tess and Maxheim. Maxheim and his brothers are on a mission to find their twin siblings that were taken from them when they were young. Maxheim is the fixer of the family and shoulders most of the burdens, guilt and stress that he thinks he has to carry. His reputation is that of a cold Alpha with a singular focus on revenge, dominance and destruction of his enemies. Until he runs into Tess at a slavers auction while looking for information. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eMaxheim who never saw himself taking a mate ends up realizing that Tess is his fated mate and he will do anything to bind her to him forever. She may also be the key to discovering more information about his lost siblings. But Tess has secrets and her own doubts about herself and her abilities. Tess' Omega gift is rare and deadly and her whole life she has been used as a pawn and a killer. Can Maxheim convince Tess that he is worth taking a chance on? Can Tess come to realize the power she carries can be used for good and embrace a bright and hopeful future with Maxheim? Will the Skolovs get closer to locating their siblings? What will happen with the changing political landscape?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis story was filled with action, secrets, revenge, heat and revelations. I adored Maxheim...he was dominant, possessive, obsessive...just how I like my alpha males. His relationship not only with his family but Tess was just so swoony I almost couldn't handle it. Maxheim taught Tess that she is more than what people have labeled her to be and deserves everything and Tess taught Maxheim that he doesn't have to carry all the pain and guilt from the past. The only thing that bothered me about this story was how stubborn Tess was and how she always wanted to resort to being the sacrificial lamb. I wanted her to grow into her own just a little faster. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOverall, if you like Omegaverse with a super alpha male that worships the ground