/book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2OYBU0T1YUXKD","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2OYBU0T1YUXKD"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/79126337?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4053791351"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.cb5KH93wY5j05HNOyrRDpg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.cb5KH93wY5j05HNOyrRDpg","creator":{"__ref":"User:79126337"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1624811547504,"createdAt":1623692371714,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1623713262776,"text":"This was my first Alison Aimes read into a genre I haven’t dipped my toes into enough, so I’d like to thank Grey’s Promo for the opportunity to explore this diverse and fascinating genre.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSavage Prince is book two in the Ruthless Warlords series. If, like me, you’re diving into the series out of sequence fear not, you’ll pick up on everything just fine without feeling like you’re floundering for information usually fed to the reader during book one.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis book when invited to read it, promised an engaging enemies-to-lovers, forced proximity, dark, mafia, sci-fi, paranormal romance. A lot to fit into one book, for sure. But not impossible. It’s all about balance to combine all of these things to produce a sensual, romantic, angsty, steamy book that quite literally, is out of this world. Alison has achieved said balance with Savage Prince.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAs promised to us in the very book title, our main male is indeed, Savage, and is by far my favourite character besides his omega. Maxheim truly is an impressively complex character, you both want to rush to his side and give him a firm lashing with your tongue at the same time. He doesn’t conform to the typical alpha-male attitude, but becomes his true self when his omega comes into his life. This gives a very human-like quality to a very inhuman like male. Simply stellar! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOne element I would like to praise especially, is the vastness and the expanse of how the story started out from caged beginnings, to where we leave the characters at the end of the book. As infinite as the sci-fi genre is, there also runs the risk of falling into the same storyline, plot and story arc. I’m always somewhat hesitant to read a sci-fi romance because of this. However, this was not the case with Savage Prince, and I couldn’t believe the places that I was taken during this read with the settings, scenes and events. More was packed into this book than the contents of Maxheim’s impressive laced trews, yet it didn’t feel overwhelming or that there was too much to digest. There was always something gripping and engaging to keep you turning those pages, rather than pausing for a breather.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI found it hard to put the book down to get a night’s sleep, as I wanted to keep journeying across the stars with our two main characters. Cannot praise Alison highly enough for reader-book engagement, fabulous work!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhich leads me onto my next point. Mystery. Just when I thought I had a plot twist figured out, I was caught completely by surprise by something that had been leaving me guessing until everything I thought I knew was turned upside down on its head. Where it’s nice to feel you can predict and guess points within the novel that will happen at a later date, it’s even more rewarding to be proven wrong, caught off guard and surprised. That, for me, is what makes a book truly interesting and I couldn’t keep my jaw closed a the moments of true shock and awe.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSavage Prince was prolific in both sad, tense, mysterious and steamy scenes that delivered so much more than the average novel. During the sad scenes, I wept tears along with our omega. During tense, angsty scenes, I was right up in my ebook shouting at our alpha as if he could hear me. During the steamy scenes, I grabbed my nearest fan an hunkered down to read some more. This is a book that truly has it all and has it all in spades, doing nothing by half measures. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eTo sum up, I’m really am glad that I took a chance on a read outside of my go-to genre. I’ve dabbled in the occasional sci-fi romance, only few of them 1% as steamy as Savage Prince, but none have left me as impressed and wanting to read more than this one. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAlison Aimes, you’ve earned yourself a new reader and one who’s looking forward to the rest of the books in this series. Five stellar stars for you!","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2OYBU0T1YUXKD\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j\"}}"},"likeCount":5,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":1},"User:3055882":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":3055882,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1785811685i/3055882._UX200_CR0,18,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":7,"textReviewsCount":1228,"name":" ~*~Princess Nya Vasiliev~*~","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/3055882-princess-nya-vasiliev","contributor":null,"id":3055882},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A27XXD127GSEP5":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A27XXD127GSEP5"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A27XXD127GSEP5\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A27XXD127GSEP5","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A27XXD127GSEP5"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-lvGUB6j"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/3055882?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8759188912"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.EG_U2CqY4IzpTdOPuTFnuQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.EG_U2CqY4IzpTdOPuTFnuQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:3055882"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1785370418928,"createdAt":1785336477578,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1785338266789,"text":"This is the 2nd book that I've read by this author.. The first book I read by her was back in 2018, and I gotta say this chick can write. She can write some down right heinous, highly charged, and sexually/emotionally intense scenes in her books.. The plot and plights are beyond intriguing and keeps you invested.. BUT-this is the 2nd book where her FMC worked my nerves to no end.. Granted this book's FMC was way better that the previous 2018 book's FMC ( I gave that book just 3 stars) but still, this one skirted the edge of \u003ci\u003eI'm too stupid \u0026amp; emotionally stunted for my own good~\u003c/i\u003e for way too long in this story, IMO... \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf you want the FMCs actions and thought processes to make sense of why she's gun shy for as long as she was here, then please DO NOT show me all this transparency in action and intention with the MMC! It annoys me to no end when the MMC is transparent about his intentions and feelings to the FMC CONSISTENTLY, in word and action, but she's still acting like she can't trust him. UGH!!! This creams my corn and pisses me off to no end!! \u003cb\u003eSTOP WRITING FEMALES LIKE THIS!\u003c/b\u003e And if you must, then make it make sense \u0026amp; be within reason! M'kay?? Thank you! Geez! \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eMaxheim Skolov- You have my heart. You have my loyalty. And you have my 💦💦💦\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSo, as you can see this FMC was why this book did not get a 5 star nod from me.. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://images.gr-assets.com/photos/1785160005p8/4504400.jpg\" width=\"400\" height=\"400\" alt=\"DBA/\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe FMC started off strong and her hesitancy in the beginning was warranted and understandable. But because so much happens back to back, and her seeing and hearing Maxheim's truth where she is concerned, to me, it took her way too long to get on board considering their set of circumstances surrounding them, and what was clearly developing between them personally..\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThat aside, this was full of mystery, heartbreak, intense action sequences and the bonds of love, loyalty, and family.. I have to say I love the original concept here of a series based in the sci-fi alien realm, but has tones of the Russian Mafia genre as well.. I've never read a fusion of genres in this way until this book.. So I really enjoyed this.. You care about the folks and their plights. The mystery and intrigue pulls you in. But you stay for the individuals and their cares that they are contending with..\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI am committed to reading the other books in this series.. I need to go back and read book 1 first, though.. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWould I recommend?=Yes\u003cbr\u003eSpice?=🌶️🌶️🌶️🌶️🌶️🌶️🌶️\u003cbr\u003ePlot/Plight?=4.5\u003cbr\u003eMCs?=It's complicated(see above)\u003cbr\u003eEnding/Epilogue?=4.5 ","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A27XXD127GSEP5\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.4TA1hhKj-l